  {
   "id": 60,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -1500,
    1180
   ],
   "size": [
    420,
    320
   ],
   "widgets_values": [
    "## wan-vace-reference.json\n\nPrompt-driven animation of a character you own (no driving clip)\n\n**Does:** VACE **reference-to-video** - your character image goes in as the **reference** and the prompt says what she should *do*; the model keeps her identity and acts it out, in the reference's own look and its plain background. Wan2.1-VACE 14B fp8_scaled (`wan2.1_vace_14B_fp8_scaled.safetensors`, 17.6 GB, **Apache-2.0**) plus the umt5 text encoder and Wan VAE this box already ships. **This is the counterpart to `wan-animate-motion.json` (S18):** that flow copies motion from a *driving clip*; this one writes the motion from *words* - the one motion source we had no route for.\n**Measured (E13b, 2026-10-10):** 81 frames at 768x768, 20 steps, cfg 6, shift 8 -> **2729 s (45.5 min)** on the 3090 at 17.25 GB VRAM. **Identity holds** on our own `char_heroine.png` across the clip, and the prompt's fire spell appears and grows in her hand (strip: `video/evidence/E13b-vace-single-strip.png`). **Two honest defects:** the gown's hem smears into a painterly swirl early, and the **last third drifts** (the action dominates, the figure softens) - keep the first ~two thirds if identity is what matters.\n**Knobs:** `length` on `WanVaceToVideo` (81 ships = 3.4 s at 24 fps; the value quantises in 4-frame chunks), **steps/cfg** on the sampler (20 / 6.0 - the 6-step distil LoRA the Animate flow uses is named for I2V at 480p and is untested with VACE reference mode), **shift** on `ModelSamplingSD3` (8.0), and the canvas (768x768 ships; 480x848 roughly halves the cost if you accept the crop).\n**Traps:** the reference brings its **background** with it - a busy photo gives a busy clip, so use a plain one. Never GGUF this model (the same metadata trap as Wan-Animate-2). And when you copy an upstream example, **audit every loader filename against what this box holds**: the example loads `wan_2.1_vae.safetensors`, which we do not have - ours is `Wan2_1_VAE_bf16.safetensors` (wired here).\n**Not in this flow yet:** several subjects at once and region placement (the reference pair and the `control_video` + `control_masks` arms) are measured in E13b and tracked there.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S28** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E13/E13b** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
